      "lineNbr": 907,
      "author": {
        "id": 3678645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-03T18:31:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In this case the check is needed, as the qindex threshold to \"enable reduced CDEF strength mode\" (qindex 220) is intentionally set up higher than the threshold to \"start zeroing out low CDEF strengths\" (qindex 140).\n\nThe intuition is that as qindex increases (and quality decreases), we need to progressively enable CDEF in more cases, with higher strengths, as ringing artifacts become more pronounced and annoying to the eye.",
      "parentUuid": "10762816_47fe0ba6",
      "revId": "cb6faf2358eef455948ddf38dcee20552084df33",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
